  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Auth identity and storage",
      "items": [
        "Auth requests use an HttpOnly JWT cookie; the backend reloads roles from PostgreSQL and enforces permissions.",
        "Auth versions, private attachment bytes/hashes, evaluation runs, decisions and audit use PostgreSQL in application code.",
        "The Auth staging Blueprint is CONFIG ONLY; the repository does not prove deployment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Inference and authority",
      "items": [
        "Inference API keys are backend-only. Adapters add Authorization: Bearer only when a key is configured.",
        "Submit calls POST /v1/chat/completions. GET /v1/models exists in VLM health_check(), but no submit-path call site was found.",
        "Backend rules choose AUTO_APPROVED or HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED; AI auto-reject is unsupported.",
        "Endpoint, tunnel and proxy are not configured by the checked-in Auth staging Blueprint; live inference is unverified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Judge Demo is separate",
      "items": [
        "Judge Demo routes use X-Demo-Actor, MockVLMProvider and a separate SQLite database.",
        "Verify uses synthetic cases and Mock providers with in-memory per-case repositories; it is not process isolation or production inference.",
        "Root Render configuration covers Judge Demo and ephemeral SQLite, not Auth PostgreSQL."
      ]
    }
  ]
